//! Sequence-based species identification for Mycobacteriaceae.
//!
//! ### Generation of species identification databases
//!
//! The reference sequences are generated by
//! [cosmic-seq](https://github.com/michaelmeuli/cosmic-seq) from the species representative
//! genomes of the [Genome Taxonomy Database (GTDB)](https://gtdb.ecogenomic.org/).
//!
//! GTDB is a genome-based bacterial and archaeal taxonomy. It groups genomes into species clusters
//! by average nucleotide identity (ANI ≥ 95 %) and places them in a phylogeny inferred from
//! 120 concatenated bacterial marker proteins (`bac120`). Each species cluster has exactly one
//! representative genome, chosen mainly by assembly quality (completeness, contamination,
//! contiguity) with a preference for type-strain genomes. The representative is therefore often,
//! but not always, the type strain. GTDB genus boundaries differ from NCBI's: for example,
//! GTDB's *Mycobacterium* also includes *Mycobacteroides* and *Mycolicibacterium*.
//!
//! cosmic-seq
//! 1. reads `bac120_metadata_r232.tsv` (GTDB release 232), keeps the rows of family
//!    `f__Mycobacteriaceae`, and of those only the rows with `gtdb_representative == t`
//!    (one genome per GTDB species, 1,812 in total, 850 of them *Mycobacterium*);
//! 2. downloads these genomes from NCBI with `datasets download genome accession`;
//! 3. runs every primer pair of the lab's Sanger assays in silico on every genome (≤ 3 mismatches
//!    per primer, IUPAC codes honoured, no gaps, both strands, product ≤ 3,000 bp) and keeps, per
//!    genome and primer pair, the products with the fewest mismatches. The product runs from the
//!    forward to the reverse primer, primers included;
//! 4. writes one FASTA per amplicon (`references/fasta/<amplicon>.fasta`; header
//!    `>accession|amplicon|N species [length=.. mismatches=f+r copies=..]`, `N` numbering the
//!    products of one genome);
//! 5. writes the species → group table `species_groups.tsv` (NCBI species groups plus curated
//!    complexes), used to name 16S calls by their complex ([`species_group`]);
//! 6. bundles both for this repository (`scripts/05_export_cosmic_files.py`), copied into
//!    `res/sequences/references/` by `scripts/sync_cosmic_seq.py`.
//!
//! `myco_erm41.fasta` is generated at build time but unused; erm41 identification uses
//! per-subspecies references (`erm41_abscessus_ATCC_19977.fasta`, `erm41_bolletii_CIP_108541.fasta`, `erm41_massiliense_CCUG_48898.fasta`) instead.

